DEFINITIONS:
[
 {
  "definition_id": "D1",
  "kind": "other",
  "text": "The model has k=16 latent states, one carried integer z, and fixed probability tables A of shape k by k and B of shape k by vocabulary size. update(x) sets z to the smallest maximizing j of A[z,j]*B[j,x]. predict returns the smallest maximizing v of sum_j A[z,j]*B[j,v]. Parameters do not change during inference. No position counter, input buffer, external memory, or additional carried state is allowed. In the architecture contract d denotes k, not an additional embedding width; there is one update round and no feed-forward expansion."
 },
 {
  "definition_id": "D2",
  "kind": "accounting",
  "text": "For cost measurement, compute the update scores by elementwise multiplication followed by argmax, and compute readout scores by the length-k vector A[z,:] @ B followed by argmax. Thus update costs k+(k-1) units and readout costs k*V+(V-1) units. Perform update and readout once per token. A and B are fixed parameters, excluded from carried state; the state object contains only z. Temporary score arrays are not retained in the state object. Generalize k to the cost grid without changing these equations."
 },
 {
  "definition_id": "D3",
  "kind": "sampling",
  "text": "Use the supplied task-contract generators and scoring positions unchanged. Copy uses D=4 and self-fed continuation, with 2*L tokens and vocabulary 5. Recall uses V=16, n_keys=2*K, 3*K+1 tokens, and vocabulary 2*K+17. Composition uses 5*T+3 tokens and vocabulary 3*T+3, with arbitrary functions and independently shuffled tables. Binding uses values=8, two interleaved chains, 4*hops+7 tokens, and vocabulary 2*hops+11. Dyck uses vocabulary 4 and the supplied variable-length balanced-word generator; measured stream lengths are 8 at depth 2, 14–16 at depth 4, 26–32 at depth 8, and 50–64 at depth 16. There is no per-token store."
 },
 {
  "definition_id": "D4",
  "kind": "evaluation",
  "text": "Learnability uses the architecture in D1 and only the card's count-based rule: decode training text with the current tables, count transitions and emissions, normalize, and repeat. The prover chooses initialization, handling of zero counts, passes, and batch organization in its declared RECIPE, without changing the architecture or learning rule. Use seeds 0, 1, 2, threshold 0.99, and 500 test instances per seed. Score copy per string, recall and composition per query, and dyck per sequence. Apply the identical learner and RECIPE to true examples, zero examples, and the same token sequences with randomized answers. Both controls and the supplied 1800-second, 4096-MB, single-core budget and replay requirements are mandatory."
 },
 {
  "definition_id": "D5",
  "kind": "notation",
  "text": "For the finite-state information statements, a source string is a function Fin L -> Fin D. enc maps the complete source prefix to its carried state, and dec maps that state to the complete self-fed continuation. Success means equality of the entire string. This includes every deterministic mechanism with only sixteen carried states; dec includes its fixed parameters and deterministic self-fed updates. Counts divided by D^L are accuracies under the uniform source distribution."
 },
 {
  "definition_id": "D6",
  "kind": "notation",
  "text": "For the recall information statement, fix any particular ordered set of K distinct keys. A value assignment is a function Fin K -> Fin V, enc is the state after storing the pairs, and dec(state,i) is the answer to key i when queried first. Average accuracy is the number of correct assignment/key combinations divided by V^K*K. Exact recall means every key is answered correctly for every assignment. The statement quantifies over all deterministic sixteen-state encoders and query decoders."
 },
 {
  "definition_id": "D7",
  "kind": "other",
  "text": "The sample-information entries use the card's declared restricted target-rule classes, supplied by the task protocol, with a uniformly drawn target and no hand-set member. For copy, recall, and composition the class is all four selectors {0,1}->{0,1}; for dyck it is all maps from the six specified nonempty depth-two stack contexts to two closers. Prior bits are zero relative to these restricted classes, not relative to a class that also learns parsing or the task protocol."
 }
]

